<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21498" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illĕcĕbrōsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inl-</span></b> ), a,
		um, adj.
		illecebra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of allurement</i>, <i>very
				enticing</i>, <i>attractive</i>, <i>seductive</i> (ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">istoc illecebrosius Fieri nihil potest,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 1, 1, 54</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sapor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. adv. Symm. 2, 144</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insidiae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 30, 1</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illĕcĕ-brōsē</span></b> , <i>enticingly</i>, <i>attractively.—Comp.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 30, 5, 7</span></i>
			 (but not in <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 3, 2, 36</span></i>; v. Ritschl ad
			h. l.).</div>
